controls_data: compare each new run with the published runs on the branches its manifest declares

A run of two branches (the D0full runs: src and def) has no orphan probes or answers, and the
anchor check listed the published anchor's orphan answers as missing on one side. The probe-set
and anchor checks now read a run's branches from params.branches (else from its answers), and a
declared branch without answers still fails both checks, so a run is neither padded nor excused.

